The real GX library runs on the host and feeds the emulated GPU. FIFO
stores go through port_gx_w8/16/32/f32 instead of volatile writes to
0xCC008000, register blocks point at the host hardware-register mirrors
(port_hw.h), the paired-single matrix/light uploads are scalar loops,
draw sync/done tokens are delivered synchronously, EFB peeks/pokes are
no-ops, colours are packed big-endian explicitly (host is little-endian)
and the FIFO read/link helpers are made non-static for the SDK layer.
J3DGD.cpp redefines GX_WRITE_U32 through GXWGFifo for the same reason.

